    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling performance today, spearheaded by **Gunnar Henderson** (79.38) and **Kyle Tucker** (76.25). **Gunnar Henderson** is our primary target for production, benefiting significantly from a favorable park factor and a matchup against Schultz, whose 5.16 xERA suggests he will struggle to suppress our elite bats. **Kyle Tucker** similarly capitalizes on the same pitching vulnerability, while **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) rounds out the top tier of our outfielders; his score is buoyed by a rare wind-out scenario and strong platoon dynamics that make him an essential start despite the moderate resistance from Rea.\n\nWe are navigating several \"Lineup Pending\" designations, most notably for **Liam Hicks**, **Andy Pages**, and **Heliot Ramos**. While **Heliot Ramos** (64.96) remains a viable play against the tough Zac Gallen due to his speed upside, our bench decision came down to a razor-thin margin between the active **Dominic Smith** (55.70) and **Brayan Rocchio** (50.99). **Brayan Rocchio** was the final cut; while his projection was respectable, the optimizer favored **Dominic Smith**\u2019s situational platoon edge against McGreevy. We are also keeping a close watch on **Sam Antonacci** (51.52), whose score is suppressed by the elite 2.22 xERA of Kremer, though his +16% park adjustment keeps him in the mix.\n\nRisks today are concentrated in the bottom third of our lineup. **Nasim Nunez** (51.23) faces a tough hurdle in Tolle, and his value is throttled by a low batting order position despite his stolen base potential. Furthermore, **Josh Jung** (59.05) remains in the \"marginal\" territory as he looks to find his footing against Cantillo. We are continuing to monitor the health status of **Jordan Westburg**, who remains sidelined, and we remain ready to pivot if official lineups significantly alter the projected plate appearances for our leadoff candidates.",
